[A10] **Owner decision, 2026-11-25 11:47: option (b). The 8x8/1if option-(a) load ceiling is raised from 0.75 to 0.76.**

The reason is in the round-4 STOP. The registration record itself costs 90-95 us per Talker, so the load would stay at 0.753 even if ACMP's per-sink completion cost nothing. The measured figure is 0.759, and the best cut reaches 0.756.

Unchanged:
- the 1x1 ceiling, 0.70;
- every other owner bound: last notice 140 ms, ACMP 30 ms, txL 49 ms, THE SHARE 2 ms.

The ceiling does not license other growth. The other rows stay at their measured values, and routed totals stay in the band.

The next round finishes #977 under that bound:
- the ceiling change in the grade;
- the gated tsn-c-stack per-sink cut, for margin;
- the hot-list relearn for the 1x1/1if AECP item;
- the every-arm runs and routes.

[A10] OWNER DECISION (2026-11-27 12:41) on item 5 of the round-10c ruling (comment 7216582862): THE TRANSMIT's stated row at 8x8/1if goes from 77 to **80 ms**, the cap named in `ctrl_loop.h`'s header. Every other bound is unchanged:
- load: 0.70 at 1x1/1if, 0.77 at 8x8/1if;
- last notice: 140 ms;
- ACMP: 30 ms;
- txL: 49 ms;
- THE SHARE: 2 ms.

The hold-off stays at 8 cs, so no image byte moves (round 10d proves this with an identity build). Round 10d keeps that commit.

[A10] OWNER DECISION (2026-11-28 08:01): the 8x8/1if load ceiling rises from 0.77 to **0.79**, for #977.

Every other bound is unchanged:
- 1x1/1if load: 0.70;
- last notice: 140 ms;
- ACMP: 30 ms;
- txL: 49 ms;
- THE SHARE: 2 ms;
- THE TRANSMIT's 8x8/1if row: 80 ms (owner decision of 2026-11-27).

Why: under the manager's decision on the deferred deliveries (comment 7229657853), the 8x8/1if load with the sourced deliveries term is 0.78214. The term is stated against the ordinary passes after the delivery window. The external review verified the figure (round 13, comment 7231383395). 1x1/1if: 0.533.

#1025 wins the margin back after the lab image, without any bound moving. PR #993's ceiling commit now cites this decision in place of "pending".
